---
title: Bread Machine Milk Bread
image: https://kimchimari.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/bread-machine-milk-bread-side-by-side.jpg
time required: 5 hours
servings: 14
cook time: 50 minutes
nutrition:
  calories: 163 kcal
  fat: 5 g
  saturated fat: 3 g
  carbohydrates: 24 g
  sugar: 5 g
  protein: 4 g
  fiber: 1 g
  sodium: 182 mg
  serving size: 14 g
course: Snack
source: https://kimchimari.com/milk-bread-bread-machine-recipe/
prep time: 10 minutes
---

Add all the wet ingredients (@milk{3/4%cup}(warm), @water{1/4%cup}(room temp), @butter{60%g}(1/4 cup approximately, unsalted, melted), @egg{1}(room temperature)) + @sea salt{1%tsp} into the #bread machine{}.

> You can add salt later with your dry ingredients but adding the salt in this step ensures it doesn't inhibit the yeast in anyway. That said if you are trying to use active dry yeast, you may want to try swapping the yeast and salt order wise so the yeast activates first.

Mix DRY ingredients - mix @bread flour{365%g}(about 2.75 cups) and @sugar{50%g} first in a bowl and then add to pan on top of the wet ingredients.

Make a little well in the middle of the dry ingredients and add @instant yeast{7%g}(1 packet, about 2tsp) inside the well and also add @milk powder{2%Tbsp}.

Put the bread pan in the machine with all the ingredients in and start a full Basic Dough cycle. 

When the dough is done, punch it down and then take the dough out of the pan onto a granite or wood cutting board and divide into 2 equal size dough. Sprinkle some flour on the surface and knead each dough a few times then shape it tightly into a ball. 

IF you have custom rise function THEN nestle each dough ball back in the bread pan next to each other and let the dough balls rise in the machine for ~{30%minutes}. IF there's NO custom rise function in your machine, you can put each dough ball into separate bowls, cover with plastic wrap or towel and let it rise in warm location or 100℉ oven for ~{20%minutes}.

Once the dough has risen, transfer the dough one at a time on a smooth surface, sprinkle surface very lightly with flour and also coat the rolling pin lightly with flour. Roll out one dough ball into a thick rectangle about 12 inches long and 4-5 inches wide. Roll the top of the dough (3 inches) down and then fold the bottom up about the same amount, resulting in a square-like dough shape. Roll it into a log, starting from one end of the square until you have a roll all rolled up.

Lightly use @butter{1%Tbsp} on the sides of the bread pan and nestle the 2 logs down in the bread machine pan.

Put pan back in the bread machine and set it to rise for ~{1%hour} or until the top of the dough is up about 70% height of the pan. Again, if you don't have custom rise function, let dough rise in the pan at room temp or in 100℉ oven for ~{40%minutes}.

Bake for ~{50%minutes}. Select the crust to your preference. Optionally, for some shine, brush the top with some milk or egg whites before baking. Note that bread baked in the bread machine won't have the same golden brown top like you get in the oven.